00:27:54.000 --> 00:27:58.000
Okay, so let's quickly run through slightly more advanced

00:27:58.000 --> 00:28:01.000
topics to finish up this video.

00:28:01.000 --> 00:28:08.000
Earlier, we mentioned that the MacBook Pro's M1 chip can complete 354 different instructions.

00:28:08.000 --> 00:28:19.000
This set of instructions is called ARMv8.4, and it's categorized by a RISC architecture or reduced instruction set computer.

00:28:19.000 --> 00:28:26.000
For example, here's a simple game of Snake using 145 lines of C++ code.

00:28:26.000 --> 00:28:31.000
It's the job of a compiler, which is a separate piece of software,

00:28:31.000 --> 00:28:36.000
to take this code along with ARMv8.4's 354 RISC instructions

00:28:36.000 --> 00:28:41.000
and generate a list of 676 assembly instructions

00:28:41.000 --> 00:28:48.000
equivalent to the machine code instructions that would be found in a book or program named snake.app.

00:28:48.000 --> 00:28:52.000
The other common architecture found in Intel and AMD chips

00:28:52.000 --> 00:28:59.000
is called CISC or complex instruction set computer and is composed of thousands of different possible

00:28:59.000 --> 00:29:06.000
instructions. For example, here's the equivalent snake program that is compiled to run on an Intel

00:29:06.000 --> 00:29:17.000
or AMD chip using CISC and x86 64-bit instructions and you can see it's only 560 instructions now.

00:29:17.000 --> 00:29:24.000
A few key differences between RISC and CISC are that each RISC instruction is relatively simple

00:29:24.000 --> 00:29:31.000
and is executed at a consistently fast execution rate. Additionally, RISC architectures are more

00:29:31.000 --> 00:29:37.000
energy efficient and thus used in all smartphones, whereas CISC architectures have thousands of

00:29:37.000 --> 00:29:44.000
different instructions and pack a lot more into a single instruction. Additionally, the CISC

00:29:44.000 --> 00:29:50.000
instruction decoder is much more complicated and individual instructions have a variable execution

00:29:50.000 --> 00:29:57.000
rate sometimes taking multiple clock cycles to execute there are many additional pros and cons

00:29:57.000 --> 00:30:03.000
to RISC versus CISC which we'll save for yet another video but we thought it worth mentioning

00:30:03.000 --> 00:30:10.000
these simplified differences here computer architecture is incredibly complicated with

00:30:10.000 --> 00:30:13.000
many different facets and layers of complexity,

00:30:13.000 --> 00:30:30.000
and we have plans to make more videos that dive into each of these topics.

00:30:30.000 --> 00:30:42.000
For example, we spent over 250 hours tearing down these non-working computers we bought from eBay and meticulously rebuilding each of the 3D models in Blender.

